<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span><span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clipping statistics under matched <math id="S4.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> We report the clipping rate <math id="S4.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{clip}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{clip}}</annotation></semantics></math> and quantiles of the clipping factor
<math id="S4.T3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Across noise multipliers, <math id="S4.T3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{clip}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{clip}}</annotation></semantics></math> remains comparable, while DP-aware slightly increases low-quantile and median values of <math id="S4.T3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, suggesting reduced clipping severity.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:320.9pt;height:35.1pt;vertical-align:-16.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-119.2pt,13.0pt) scale(0.573711499271642,0.573711499271642) ;">
<table id="S4.T4.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
